{# BREADCRUMB — replaces the site logo in the top-left. The trail comes from the global `breadcrumbs` computed data (src/_data/eleventyComputed.js), shared with schemas/BreadcrumbList.njk so the visible trail and the structured data never drift. Standalone: it does NOT depend on the main nav existing.

   - Home crumb = the logomark (orange loop SVG) linking to /, with a visually-hidden name for screen readers and crawlers.
   - Intermediate crumbs = section archives, plain links.
   - Final crumb = the current page, plain text, aria-current="page", never a link. Its label is rendered through partials/breadcrumb-leaf.njk (per-type, e.g. the Jam "song by artist" treatment).
   Separators are drawn in CSS (breadcrumb.css), so assistive tech never reads them. #}

<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumb">
  <ol class="cluster" role="list">
    {% for crumb in breadcrumbs %}
      <li>
        {% if crumb.isHome %}
          <a
            href="/"
            class="breadcrumb-home"
            {%- if crumb.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}
          >
            {% svg "misc/logo" %}
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{ meta.siteName }}, home</span>
          </a>
        {% elif crumb.current %}
          <span class="breadcrumb-current" aria-current="page">
            {% include "partials/breadcrumb-leaf.njk" %}
          </span>
        {% else %}
          <a href="{{ crumb.url }}">{{ crumb.label }}</a>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</nav>
